1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,180
Quentin Tarantino, one of the most acclaimed filmmakers of all time, known for bringing his bold ideas to life with surreal visuals and mind-bending storytelling.

2
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:10,560
But he wasn't always a Hollywood icon.

3
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:13,780
Once he was just an ordinary guy working at a video store.

4
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:16,960
Until one night he decided to rewrite his story.

5
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:46,100
Today I present you the Tarantino method.

6
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:48,560
To follow this process, you'll need three things.

7
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,1000
A pen, a notepad, and the dead of night.

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,140
When the world is silent and now the soul is awake.

9
00:00:54,140 --> 00:00:56,140
That's when it can happen. Trust.

10
00:00:56,140 --> 00:00:57,260
Now it begins.

11
00:00:57,260 --> 00:01:03,180
The first page is always going to be the hardest, but it's really all about getting that ball rolling.

12
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:24,107
Now that you started you have to ask yourself the big scary fear monger what am I doing wrong Be brutally honest as Quinton himself would say nail it Take your time Dive deep It gritty It tough But it absolutely necessary And when you push through boom you halfway there

13
00:01:24,107 --> 00:01:27,687
It's all out there.

14
00:01:27,687 --> 00:01:33,987
The fears, the doubts, the mistakes, the lessons, the heartbreak, all laid out, bare for you to see.

15
00:01:33,987 --> 00:01:37,587
Not built up in your mind, but on paper. Tangible.

16
00:01:37,587 --> 00:01:43,687
Take a moment, because now you have to ask yourself, how can I change it?

17
00:01:43,687 --> 00:01:45,987
We're not all Quentin Tarantino.

18
00:01:45,987 --> 00:01:48,347
You might be feeling like you're all written out.

19
00:01:48,347 --> 00:01:50,347
So let's make this part simple.

20
00:01:50,347 --> 00:01:51,767
A straightforward list.

21
00:01:51,767 --> 00:01:54,187
A hundred ways you can change your life.

22
00:01:54,187 --> 00:02:00,187
Quite a simple process. Take a mistake you've learned and write down a way to change it. Repeat it.

23
00:02:00,187 --> 00:02:06,587
Over and over again and push forward. Write it down. Adapt. Reflect. Learn. Learn.

24
00:02:06,587 --> 00:02:10,347
Until finally, when you ask yourself, how can I change my life?

25
00:02:10,347 --> 00:02:11,807
You'll have a hundred ways to do it.

26
00:02:11,807 --> 00:02:15,487
But there's one very important thing you need to remember throughout this whole night.

27
00:02:15,487 --> 00:02:17,487
You gotta actually f***ing do it.
